      "prompt": "Use the referenced Echo Catwalk art only to preserve his exact identity and colors. Create eight new full-body poses for a right-facing reverse layup, on a 1536\u00d71024 transparent RGBA pixel-art sheet in a strict four-column by two-row grid, row-major. Broad transparent margins around every complete figure. No backgrounds, court, hoop, floor, text, ball, props or shadows.\n\nEcho is a compact adult human male athlete, medium-brown skin, short spiky dark-teal curls, teal headband, neat dark-teal beard, teal jersey and shorts with black/deep-purple panels, black knee pads, teal-black shoes and wristbands. Keep same male face, human proportions and kit in every pose. Two arms/hands, two legs/shoes. Hands remain empty; game renders the separate ball.\n\nRight-facing reverse layup toward an offscreen hoop at image-right. Sequence:\n0 approach in a controlled stride;\n1 gather invisible ball at chest;\n2 plant and load;\n3 jump and turn shoulders away from the rim, ball-miming hand sweeps behind far shoulder;\n4 rise with back/shoulder leading, other arm counterbalances;\n5 RELEASE at simulation tick12: reverse-side arm reaches high backward over the shoulder, open empty hand, knees tucked;\n6 empty-handed follow-through and controlled descent;\n7 balanced landing and recovery.\n\nMake all eight distinct, connected and full-body, keep complete hair and shoes in cells, with the whole pose readable. No ball or props at all. True transparent alpha-zero exterior and gutters, no halo, checkerboard or matte. Crisp arcade pixel-art clusters, small-sprite readability. Return only the sheet.",
